## Contractors

wf-contractor-cael-port = Caelestinus Port Authority
wf-contractor-cael-port-desc = Runs the sector's mail and freight out of Caelestinus Central.
wf-contractor-cael-marshals = Caelestinus Marshals
wf-contractor-cael-marshals-desc = Keeps the lanes around Central clear of the people who make them dangerous.
wf-contractor-mmc = Mieyo Manufacturing Concern
wf-contractor-mmc-desc = MMC Hokkaido buys ore by the crate and pays to keep its claims its own.
wf-contractor-sevastopol = Sevastopol Data Storage
wf-contractor-sevastopol-desc = Keeps the sector's records, and wants its data moved by hand and never read.
wf-contractor-stellar-blessing = Stellar Blessing Colony Board
wf-contractor-stellar-blessing-desc = A colony ship of TSF civilians that needs everything a new settlement needs.
wf-contractor-halcyon = TSFMC Logistics Command
wf-contractor-halcyon-desc = Supplies the Marine Corps aboard the Halcyon, and pays crews that thin out the pirates.
wf-contractor-camelot = Camelot Harbourmaster
wf-contractor-camelot-desc = Keeps Freeport Camelot fed, fuelled and trading, a long way from anywhere.
wf-contractor-anomalous-lab = Anomalous Lab Directorate
wf-contractor-anomalous-lab-desc = The sector's research station; pays well for anything strange, intact and delivered.

## Bounty targets

wf-contract-target-skip = Bail jumper {$designation}
wf-contract-target-data-thief = Data thief {$designation}
wf-contract-target-claim-jumper = Claim jumpers {$designation}
wf-contract-target-smuggler = Smuggler {$designation}
wf-contract-target-raider-pair = Raider pair {$designation}
wf-contract-target-gunship = Raider gunship {$designation}
wf-contract-target-warlord = Warlord {$designation}

wf-contract-goods-anomaly-core = anomaly cores

## Caelestinus Port Authority

wf-contract-cael-parcel-run = Parcel run to {$destination}
wf-contract-cael-parcel-run-brief = {$count ->
    [one] A sealed parcel is waiting at the board for {$destination}.
   *[other] {$count} sealed parcels are waiting at the board for {$destination}.
} Hand-carried; any shuttle will do. {$count ->
    [one] Walk it aboard the station and it's signed for.
   *[other] Walk them aboard the station and they're signed for.
}

wf-contract-cael-priority-mail = Priority mail for {$destination}
wf-contract-cael-priority-mail-brief = {$count} priority parcels for {$destination}, {$km} km out. The clock is short and the addressees are impatient. A quick shuttle is worth more than a big one here.

wf-contract-cael-fragile = Fragile goods to {$destination}
wf-contract-cael-fragile-brief = {$count ->
    [one] A fragile parcel goes
   *[other] {$count} fragile parcels go
} to {$destination}. {$count ->
    [one] It is insured, so a deposit is taken against it. Don't get into a fight with it in your bag.
   *[other] They are insured, so a deposit is taken against them. Don't get into a fight with them in your bag.
}

wf-contract-cael-general-freight = General freight to {$destination}
wf-contract-cael-general-freight-brief = {$count} crates of general stores for {$destination}, {$km} km out. They need a hold or a lot of patience: load them at the board, fly them over, and drag them onto the station.

wf-contract-cael-inbound-freight = Freight pickup at {$origin}
wf-contract-cael-inbound-freight-brief = {$count} crates of machine parts are sitting at {$origin} with Central's name on them. Collect them there and bring them back to Caelestinus Central. You'll need a hold.

wf-contract-cael-bulk-freight = Bulk freight to {$destination}
wf-contract-cael-bulk-freight-brief = {$count} heavy equipment crates for {$destination}, {$km} km out. This is a job for a real freighter; a light shuttle will crawl. A deposit is held against the cargo.

wf-contract-cael-luxury-convoy = Insured convoy to {$destination}
wf-contract-cael-luxury-convoy-brief = {$count} crates of luxury goods for {$destination}, worth more than most ships that will carry them. The insurer wants a large deposit and expects you to arrive. Bring escorts if you have friends.

wf-contract-cael-station-stores = Station stores for Central
wf-contract-cael-station-stores-brief = Central's maintenance crews are short of stock: {$goods}. Pack them into the manifest crate at the board and close it anywhere aboard the station.

wf-contract-cael-medical-stock = Medical stock for Central
wf-contract-cael-medical-stock-brief = The infirmary is running low: {$goods}. Buy, make or find them, pack the manifest crate and close it aboard Central.

## Caelestinus Marshals

wf-contract-marshal-skip = Bail jumper near {$home}
wf-contract-marshal-skip-brief = {$target} skipped a hearing and is drifting about {$km} km from {$home} in an unarmed shuttle. They won't fight, but they will run. Disable or destroy the shuttle; a gun or a boarding party will do.

wf-contract-marshal-smuggler = Smuggler run near {$home}
wf-contract-marshal-smuggler-brief = {$target} is moving contraband through the lanes around {$home} in a lightly armed runner. Expect them to run and to shoot back. Destroy the ship.

wf-contract-marshal-raiders = Raider pair near {$home}
wf-contract-marshal-raiders-brief = Two raiders are working a lane about {$km} km out from {$home} and firing on anyone who comes close. Both hulls have to go. Bring a gunboat or a friend.

wf-contract-marshal-gunship = Raider gunship near {$home}
wf-contract-marshal-gunship-brief = A Reaver gunship with a boarding crew is holding a lane about {$km} km out from {$home}. This needs a crewed, armed ship. The Marshals take a deposit so they know you mean it.

wf-contract-marshal-warlord = Warlord sighted near {$home}
wf-contract-marshal-warlord-brief = {$target} is sitting about {$km} km out from {$home} in a heavy warship with a veteran crew. Only take this with a warship and a crew to match. Whatever is left of the hull is yours to claim.

wf-contract-marshal-evidence = Evidence recovery
wf-contract-marshal-evidence-brief = A smuggler's hulk has turned up about {$km} km out from {$home}. Its cargo manifest is evidence in a case the Marshals would like to close. Find it aboard the wreck and bring it to the board. The wreck may not be empty.

## Mieyo Manufacturing Concern

wf-contract-mmc-iron-quota = Iron quota for Hokkaido
wf-contract-mmc-iron-quota-brief = MMC's smelters want {$goods}. Mine it, pack the manifest crate from the board, and close it aboard Hokkaido. Any mining shuttle can do this.

wf-contract-mmc-bulk-minerals = Bulk minerals for Hokkaido
wf-contract-mmc-bulk-minerals-brief = Hokkaido's process lines need {$goods}. Pack the manifest crate and close it aboard Hokkaido.

wf-contract-mmc-precious-ore = Precious ore for Hokkaido
wf-contract-mmc-precious-ore-brief = MMC is buying {$goods} above market. Metallic rocks further out hold the most. Pack the manifest crate and close it aboard Hokkaido.

wf-contract-mmc-plasma-ore = Plasma ore for Hokkaido
wf-contract-mmc-plasma-ore-brief = The refinery is starved of plasma: {$goods}. Pack the manifest crate and close it aboard Hokkaido.

wf-contract-mmc-lithium = Lithium contract
wf-contract-mmc-lithium-brief = MMC needs {$goods} for cell production, and lithium is scarce. It is found in chromite asteroids. Pack the manifest crate and close it aboard Hokkaido.

wf-contract-mmc-rare-ore = Rare ore order
wf-contract-mmc-rare-ore-brief = A board-level order: {$goods}. Expect a long search. Pack the manifest crate and close it aboard Hokkaido.

wf-contract-mmc-refined = Refined stock for Hokkaido
wf-contract-mmc-refined-brief = MMC's fabricators want finished stock: {$goods}. Smelt it, buy it or print it. Pack the manifest crate and close it aboard Hokkaido.

wf-contract-mmc-machine-parts = Machine parts for Hokkaido
wf-contract-mmc-machine-parts-brief = {$count} crates of drill and conveyor parts are waiting at the board for Hokkaido, {$km} km out. They need a hold.

wf-contract-mmc-claim-jumpers = Claim jumpers near Hokkaido
wf-contract-mmc-claim-jumpers-brief = {$target} have parked a gun-fitted hull on an MMC claim about {$km} km from Hokkaido and warn off anyone who comes near. Remove them. A lightly armed civilian ship can do it if it doesn't sit still.

wf-contract-mmc-survey-recorder = Lost survey craft
wf-contract-mmc-survey-recorder-brief = An MMC survey craft went quiet about {$km} km out from Hokkaido. Recover its flight recorder from the wreck and bring it to Hokkaido.

## Sevastopol Data Storage

wf-contract-sev-data-courier = Data courier to {$destination}
wf-contract-sev-data-courier-brief = {$count ->
    [one] An encrypted data case is
   *[other] {$count} encrypted data cases are
} ready at Sevastopol for {$destination}. Collect at Sevastopol, carry by hand, deliver aboard {$destination}.

wf-contract-sev-data-inbound = Archive transfer to Sevastopol
wf-contract-sev-data-inbound-brief = {$count ->
    [one] A data case at the board is
   *[other] {$count} data cases at the board are
} bound for Sevastopol's archive, {$km} km out. Hand-carried; any shuttle will do.

wf-contract-sev-secure-transfer = Secure transfer to {$destination}
wf-contract-sev-secure-transfer-brief = {$count} encrypted cases from Sevastopol to {$destination}, on a tight clock. The deposit covers what the data is worth to the wrong people. Don't stop for anything.

wf-contract-sev-server-racks = Server racks for Sevastopol
wf-contract-sev-server-racks-brief = {$count} crates of rack hardware are waiting at the board for Sevastopol, {$km} km out. They need a hold.

wf-contract-sev-hardware = Hardware for Sevastopol
wf-contract-sev-hardware-brief = Sevastopol's technicians need {$goods}. Pack the manifest crate from the board and close it aboard Sevastopol.

wf-contract-sev-core-recovery = Data core recovery
wf-contract-sev-core-recovery-brief = A ship carrying Sevastopol storage cores broke up about {$km} km out from the station. Telemetry says one core survived. Find it in the wreck and bring it home before someone else reads it.

wf-contract-sev-data-thief = Data thief near Sevastopol
wf-contract-sev-data-thief-brief = {$target} walked out of Sevastopol with an archive and is running in an unarmed shuttle with one hired gun. Stop the ship; the data is not to leave the sector.

## Stellar Blessing Colony Board

wf-contract-sb-colony-stores = Colony stores
wf-contract-sb-colony-stores-brief = The colony is short of {$goods}. Pack the manifest crate from the board and close it aboard the Stellar Blessing. A good first contract: the colony is next door to Central.

wf-contract-sb-construction = Building stock for the colony
wf-contract-sb-construction-brief = The colony is building out: {$goods}. Pack the manifest crate and close it aboard the Stellar Blessing.

wf-contract-sb-settler-mail = Settlers' mail to {$destination}
wf-contract-sb-settler-mail-brief = {$count ->
    [one] A parcel from the colonists is
   *[other] {$count} parcels from the colonists are
} waiting aboard the Stellar Blessing for {$destination}. Hand-carried; any shuttle will do.

wf-contract-sb-inbound-supplies = Supplies for the colony
wf-contract-sb-inbound-supplies-brief = {$count} crates of colony stores are waiting at the board. Haul them over to the Stellar Blessing; it is close, but they need a hold or a long drag.

wf-contract-sb-medical-relief = Medical relief from {$origin}
wf-contract-sb-medical-relief-brief = {$origin} has {$count} crates of medical supplies set aside for the colony. Collect them there and bring them to the Stellar Blessing.

wf-contract-sb-ore-quota = Ore for the colony foundry
wf-contract-sb-ore-quota-brief = The colony foundry wants {$goods}. Pack the manifest crate and close it aboard the Stellar Blessing.

wf-contract-sb-lost-shuttle = Missing colony shuttle
wf-contract-sb-lost-shuttle-brief = A colonists' shuttle went missing about {$km} km from the Stellar Blessing. The colonists' families want to know what happened. Bring back its flight recorder.

## TSFMC Logistics Command

wf-contract-tsf-munitions = Munitions run to the Halcyon
wf-contract-tsf-munitions-brief = {$count} crates of munitions for the Halcyon, {$km} km out. They're heavy and they make you a target. A deposit is held against the load.

wf-contract-tsf-reactor-parts = Reactor parts for the Halcyon
wf-contract-tsf-reactor-parts-brief = {$count} crates of reactor components for the Halcyon's engineers. Each is bulk cargo: bring a freighter with a strong drive, and friends.

wf-contract-tsf-dispatches = Sealed dispatches to {$destination}
wf-contract-tsf-dispatches-brief = {$count ->
    [one] A sealed dispatch
   *[other] {$count} sealed dispatches
} from the Halcyon for {$destination}. The clock is short. Collect {$count ->
    [one] it
   *[other] them
} aboard the Halcyon and carry {$count ->
    [one] it
   *[other] them
} by hand.

wf-contract-tsf-med-supply = Field medical supply
wf-contract-tsf-med-supply-brief = The Corps' medics need {$goods}. Pack the manifest crate from the board and close it aboard the Halcyon.

wf-contract-tsf-armour-stock = Armour stock for the Halcyon
wf-contract-tsf-armour-stock-brief = The Halcyon's fabricators want {$goods} for plating and munitions. Pack the manifest crate and close it aboard the Halcyon.

wf-contract-tsf-raiders = Pirate sweep
wf-contract-tsf-raiders-brief = Two raiders are preying on traffic about {$km} km from the Halcyon. The Corps would rather pay a contractor than divert a patrol. Destroy both.

wf-contract-tsf-gunship = Gunship interdiction
wf-contract-tsf-gunship-brief = A Reaver gunship with a boarding crew is about {$km} km out from the Halcyon. Crewed, armed ships only. Destroy it.

wf-contract-tsf-recorder = Downed patrol recorder
wf-contract-tsf-recorder-brief = A patrol craft was lost about {$km} km out from the Halcyon. Command wants its flight recorder back before anyone else listens to it. Expect the wreck to be dangerous.

## Camelot Harbourmaster

wf-contract-camelot-provisions = Provisions for Camelot
wf-contract-camelot-provisions-brief = The freeport's galleys need {$goods}. Pack the manifest crate from the board and close it aboard Camelot, {$km} km out.

wf-contract-camelot-fuel = Reactor fuel for Camelot
wf-contract-camelot-fuel-brief = Camelot's reactors are running thin. Bring {$goods} in the manifest crate and close it aboard Camelot, {$km} km out.

wf-contract-camelot-scrap-stock = Repair stock for Camelot
wf-contract-camelot-scrap-stock-brief = The freeport is held together by whatever arrives: {$goods}. Pack the manifest crate and close it aboard Camelot.

wf-contract-camelot-long-haul = Long haul to Camelot
wf-contract-camelot-long-haul-brief = {$count} crates of stores for Freeport Camelot, {$km} km out. A long trip through open space: bring fuel and a hold.

wf-contract-camelot-exports = Camelot exports to {$destination}
wf-contract-camelot-exports-brief = {$count} crates of the freeport's finest exports are waiting at Camelot for {$destination}. Collect them at Camelot and deliver them with seals intact.

wf-contract-camelot-parcel = Freeport mail to {$destination}
wf-contract-camelot-parcel-brief = {$count ->
    [one] A parcel at Camelot is
   *[other] {$count} parcels at Camelot are
} addressed to {$destination}. Hand-carried.

wf-contract-camelot-smuggler = Smuggler near Camelot
wf-contract-camelot-smuggler-brief = {$target} has been undercutting the freeport's traders with stolen goods. They fly a light runner near Camelot and shoot back. Destroy the ship.

wf-contract-camelot-manifest = Lost freighter's manifest
wf-contract-camelot-manifest-brief = A freighter bound for Camelot never arrived. Its wreck is about {$km} km out. Recover the cargo manifest for the insurers and bring it to Camelot.

## Anomalous Lab Directorate

wf-contract-lab-samples = Sample courier to {$destination}
wf-contract-lab-samples-brief = {$count ->
    [one] A sealed sample case
   *[other] {$count} sealed sample cases
} from the Anomalous Lab for {$destination}. Collect at the Lab. {$count ->
    [one] It hums.
   *[other] They hum.
} That is normal.

wf-contract-lab-instruments = Instruments for the Lab
wf-contract-lab-instruments-brief = {$count} crates of instruments and reagents are waiting at the board for the Anomalous Lab, {$km} km out. They need a hold.

wf-contract-lab-cores = Anomaly cores wanted
wf-contract-lab-cores-brief = The Lab wants {$goods}, any kind, intact. Pack the manifest crate from the board and close it aboard the Anomalous Lab.

wf-contract-lab-fragments = Artifact fragments wanted
wf-contract-lab-fragments-brief = The Lab is reconstructing an artifact and needs {$goods}. Salvage turns them up. Pack the manifest crate and close it aboard the Anomalous Lab.

wf-contract-lab-materials = Lab materials
wf-contract-lab-materials-brief = The Lab's fabricators need {$goods}. Pack the manifest crate and close it aboard the Anomalous Lab.

wf-contract-lab-exotic-ore = Exotic ore for the Lab
wf-contract-lab-exotic-ore-brief = The Lab is paying for {$goods}. The far belts are the place to look. Pack the manifest crate and close it aboard the Anomalous Lab.

wf-contract-lab-anomaly-sample = Anomalous wreck
wf-contract-lab-anomaly-sample-brief = Something in a wreck about {$km} km from the Lab is giving off readings it should not. Recover the sample canister and bring it to the Lab. Handle with care.

## Escort runs

wf-contract-escort-quiet = Trader {$designation}
wf-contract-escort-light = Freighter {$designation}
wf-contract-escort-heavy = Convoy freighter {$designation}

wf-contract-cael-escort-trader = Shepherd a trader to {$destination}
wf-contract-cael-escort-trader-brief = A nervous independent trader won't fly to {$destination} ({$km} km) alone. Meet {$target} at the rendezvous near {$home} and stay with it until it docks. Nobody is known to be after it; any ship will do.

wf-contract-cael-escort-freighter = Freighter escort to {$destination}
wf-contract-cael-escort-freighter-brief = {$target} is carrying Port Authority freight to {$destination}, {$km} km out, and a raider has been seen on that lane. Meet it at the rendezvous and see it there. It waits for you; a light gunboat can handle this.

wf-contract-cael-escort-convoy = Convoy escort to {$destination}
wf-contract-cael-escort-convoy-brief = A heavy freighter bound for {$destination} has attracted a two-ship raid: one raider early, a gunship later. Bring a crew and something with real guns. The freighter must arrive.

wf-contract-mmc-escort-ore-hauler = Ore hauler escort to {$destination}
wf-contract-mmc-escort-ore-hauler-brief = An MMC ore hauler is taking a load to {$destination} and pirates know it. Meet {$target} near Hokkaido and keep it alive until it docks.

wf-contract-camelot-escort-trader = Freeport trader escort to {$destination}
wf-contract-camelot-escort-trader-brief = A Camelot trader is making the long run to {$destination} ({$km} km) with a raider on its tail. Meet it near the freeport and bring it in.

wf-contract-tsf-escort-supply = Corps supply convoy to {$destination}
wf-contract-tsf-escort-supply-brief = A Marine Corps supply freighter is bound for {$destination} and two raiders mean to have it. The Corps would rather pay you than pull a patrol. Bring a crewed gunship.

## Faction boards

wf-contractor-tsf-requisitions = TSF Naval Requisitions
wf-contractor-tsf-requisitions-desc = Federation work for Federation people, paid in thalers and Federation credits.
wf-contractor-ussp-commissariat = USSP Commissariat
wf-contractor-ussp-commissariat-desc = The freeport's own needs, posted for its citizens at good rates.
wf-contractor-pdv-quartermaster = PDV Quartermaster
wf-contractor-pdv-quartermaster-desc = Prizes and stores wanted at Helios, paid in thalers and doubloons.

wf-contract-tsf-faction-patrol = Lane patrol near the Halcyon
wf-contract-tsf-faction-patrol-brief = Naval Requisitions wants {$target} cleared off a Federation lane about {$km} km from the Halcyon. Federation personnel and civilians only. Paid in thalers and Federation credits.

wf-contract-tsf-faction-sweep = Pirate sweep for the Navy
wf-contract-tsf-faction-sweep-brief = Two raiders have been hitting Federation traffic about {$km} km out. Destroy both. Paid in thalers and Federation credits.

wf-contract-tsf-faction-materiel = War materiel for the Halcyon
wf-contract-tsf-faction-materiel-brief = The Corps needs {$goods}. Pack the manifest crate and close it aboard the Halcyon. The Dynasty and the Commissariat will hear who supplied it.

wf-contract-tsf-faction-colony-run = Navy stores to the colony
wf-contract-tsf-faction-colony-run-brief = {$count} crates of Navy stores are waiting aboard the Halcyon for the Stellar Blessing colony. Collect them there and haul them over.

wf-contract-tsf-faction-convoy = Federation convoy escort
wf-contract-tsf-faction-convoy-brief = A Federation freighter is bound for {$destination} with a raider waiting. Meet it near the Halcyon and see it home.

wf-contract-tsf-faction-recorder = Lost patrol recorder
wf-contract-tsf-faction-recorder-brief = A Federation patrol craft went down about {$km} km from the Halcyon. Bring its flight recorder back before the Dynasty finds it.

wf-contract-ussp-faction-rations = Rations for the freeport
wf-contract-ussp-faction-rations-brief = The Commissariat needs {$goods} for the freeport's canteens. Pack the manifest crate and close it aboard Camelot. For USSP citizens only.

wf-contract-ussp-faction-reactor = Reactor fuel for the freeport
wf-contract-ussp-faction-reactor-brief = Camelot's reactors run on what its citizens bring: {$goods}. Pack the manifest crate and close it aboard Camelot. The Federation won't like it.

wf-contract-ussp-faction-defence = Defend the freeport lanes
wf-contract-ussp-faction-defence-brief = Two raiders are preying on ships making for Camelot, about {$km} km out. Destroy both. The Commissariat pays its own well.

wf-contract-ussp-faction-smugglers = Smuggler undercutting the freeport
wf-contract-ussp-faction-smugglers-brief = {$target} is undercutting the freeport's traders. Destroy the ship.

wf-contract-ussp-faction-convoy = Freeport convoy escort
wf-contract-ussp-faction-convoy-brief = A freeport freighter is making the long run to {$destination} ({$km} km) with a raider waiting. Meet it near Camelot and bring it through.

wf-contract-pdv-faction-prize = Prize near Helios
wf-contract-pdv-faction-prize-brief = {$target} is sitting about {$km} km from Helios with a hold worth taking. Take the ship. Dynasty crews only. Paid in thalers and doubloons.

wf-contract-pdv-faction-rivals = Rival raiders on Dynasty ground
wf-contract-pdv-faction-rivals-brief = Two raiders who answer to nobody are hunting near Helios, about {$km} km out. Show them whose ground it is. Paid in thalers and doubloons.

wf-contract-pdv-faction-armoury = Stores for the Helios armoury
wf-contract-pdv-faction-armoury-brief = The Quartermaster wants {$goods}. Pack the manifest crate and close it aboard Helios. The Federation will remember who armed us.

wf-contract-pdv-faction-salvage = Plunder recovery
wf-contract-pdv-faction-salvage-brief = A freighter's wreck is drifting about {$km} km from Helios. Its cargo manifest says where the rest of the convoy went. Bring it to Helios.

## Crew work: quotas too big for one shuttle, priced for a crew.

wf-contract-mmc-bulk-ore = Bulk ore run for Hokkaido
wf-contract-mmc-bulk-ore-brief = MMC is short on feedstock for a full smelter shift and wants {$goods}. Too much for one miner: bring a crew, pack the manifest crate from the board and close it aboard Hokkaido.
wf-contract-mmc-deep-core = Deep core haul
wf-contract-mmc-deep-core-brief = A forward contract MMC can't fill from its own claims: {$goods}. Needs a crew of two working rock together. Pack the manifest crate and close it aboard Hokkaido.
wf-contract-mmc-strip-claim = Strip a claim for MMC
wf-contract-mmc-strip-claim-brief = MMC has bought out a claim and wants it stripped bare before the lease runs out: {$goods}. A full mining crew's work. Pack the manifest crate and close it aboard Hokkaido.
wf-contract-sb-foundation = Foundation pour for the colony
wf-contract-sb-foundation-brief = The Colony Board is laying a new habitat deck and needs {$goods} all at once. Buy, print or refine them as a crew, pack the manifest crate and close it aboard the Stellar Blessing.
wf-contract-sb-colony-ore = Colony ore drive
wf-contract-sb-colony-ore-brief = The colony's fabricators run on raw ore and they are nearly dry. Bring {$goods} with a crew, packed in the manifest crate and closed aboard the Stellar Blessing.
wf-contract-tsf-faction-ore = Fleet ore requisition
wf-contract-tsf-faction-ore-brief = Naval Requisitions needs {$goods} for the fleet's yards. Crew work, for Federation personnel and civilians only. Close the manifest crate aboard the Halcyon. Paid in thalers and Federation credits.
wf-contract-ussp-faction-ore = Commissariat ore quota
wf-contract-ussp-faction-ore-brief = The Commissariat sets the quota and the brigade meets it: {$goods}, closed in the manifest crate aboard Camelot. Crew work, for USSP citizens only.

## Science: anomaly surveys.

wf-contract-lab-survey = Anomaly survey
wf-contract-lab-survey-brief = Survey drones picked up {$count ->
        [one] an anomaly
       *[other] {$count} anomalies
    } aboard a derelict about {$km} km from the Lab. Fly out and scan {$count ->
        [one] it
       *[other] each one
    } with an anomaly scanner before {$count ->
        [one] it collapses
       *[other] any of them collapse
    }. Scanners are in the contractor tool loadout and on any protolathe.
wf-contract-lab-infested-hulk = Infested hulk survey
wf-contract-lab-infested-hulk-brief = A hulk about {$km} km from the Lab has gone over to flesh: {$count} anomalies are feeding whatever is crawling around in there. Bring a crew, cut through the infestation and scan every anomaly aboard before one goes critical.
wf-contract-lab-xeno-nest = Xeno nest survey
wf-contract-lab-xeno-nest-brief = The Directorate has found a xeno nest grown around {$count} anomalies, about {$km} km from the Lab. They want readings from every one of them, and the nest will not make that easy. Armed crews only.
wf-contract-sev-signal-survey = Signal source survey
wf-contract-sev-signal-survey-brief = Sevastopol's arrays are picking up interference from a derelict about {$km} km out. Scan the {$count ->
        [one] anomaly
       *[other] {$count} anomalies
    } aboard with an anomaly scanner so the archive can filter it out. Carp have been seen around it.
wf-contract-tsf-faction-anomaly = Anomalous contact
wf-contract-tsf-faction-anomaly-brief = A patrol logged {$count} anomalies and hostile life aboard a derelict about {$km} km from the Halcyon. Naval Intelligence wants every one scanned before they destabilise. Crew work, for Federation personnel and civilians only. Paid in thalers and Federation credits.

## Tows: bring a derelict hull in.

wf-contract-cael-clear-lane = Clear a derelict from the lanes
wf-contract-cael-clear-lane-brief = A dead hull is drifting about {$km} km out from Central, across an approach lane. The Port Authority wants it towed in where it can be broken up. Bring it in by tether, in one piece. Towing takes a rope coil and a tether installer; bring both to take the job.
wf-contract-sb-scrap-hull = Scrap hull for the colony
wf-contract-sb-scrap-hull-brief = The colony's recyclers can turn a wreck into a season of plating. Tow the derelict about {$km} km out from the Stellar Blessing back to the colony. Carp have been nesting in it. Towing takes a rope coil and a tether installer; bring both to take the job.
wf-contract-mmc-hauler-hull = Recover a lost ore hauler
wf-contract-mmc-hauler-hull-brief = One of MMC's haulers lost power about {$km} km from Hokkaido and its crew got out. MMC wants the hull back for refit. Tow it to Hokkaido intact. Towing takes a rope coil and a tether installer; bring both to take the job.
wf-contract-camelot-prize-hull = Prize hull for Camelot
wf-contract-camelot-prize-hull-brief = The Harbourmaster has a buyer for a hull drifting about {$km} km from Camelot, if someone can bring it in. Something has taken root aboard. Bring a crew, clear what you must and tow the hull into the harbour. Towing takes a rope coil and a tether installer; bring both to take the job.

